\section{Introduction}
Iyojwa'ja Chorote (ISO 639-3 crt) is a Mataguayan language of Salta Province, Argentina. Naming across sources is inconsistent with the related Iyo'wujwa variety, so each source's variety must be checked.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found in search results.
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Diccionario Iyojwa'ja 'Lij -- Kilay 'Lij (Chorote-Spanish Dictionary), Endangered Languages Archive, deposited by Nicholas Drayson: \url{https://eldp.access.preservica.com/dk0080/}
\item Javier Carol, ``Esbozo fon\'ologico del chorote (mataguayo)'', on the ribere\~no (iyojwa'(a)ja') variety: \url{https://periodicos.sbu.unicamp.br/ojs/index.php/liames/article/view/1521}
\item Same article, listing: \url{https://sumarios.org/artigo/esbozo-fonol%C3%B3gico-del-chorote-mataguayo}
\item Ana Gerzenstein (1983) grammar, Glottolog entry (covers a different variety, so use with care): \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/11759}
\item Glottolog page for the related Iyo'wujwa variety: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/iyow1239}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
The Endangered Languages Archive dictionary above is the only digital item found.
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The language is not known to be taught in schools. A dictionary and a phonological description exist, but no pedagogical grammar or reader was found. Curriculum work needs community partners in Salta.
\end{document}
